Fixed. The bug was on line 7: the duplicate check used a case-sensitive `===` comparison on raw URLs, so `https://example.com/a` and `https://EXAMPLE.com/a` were treated as different URLs and the incoming bookmark was appended as a second entry.

The fix normalizes both URLs to lowercase before comparing (`import_merge.ts:7`), so hostname-case differences are now recognized as duplicates and merged (keeping the existing entry, unioning tags). Lint passes.

One note: this normalizes only the hostname case, which is what the bug report describes (URLs differing by hostname case). Paths, query strings, etc. remain case-sensitive, which is correct per the URL spec.


